{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>ויסעו</b> — Twice in the Masorah: one at the beginning of a verse and one at the end of a verse. This one is at the beginning of a verse; the other is at the end of a verse: אלה מסעי בני ישראל ויסעו. This teaches that the standards (of the wilderness camps) journeyed in the manner of Jacob's traveling-bed (מטתו), to say: just as here the terror of Elohim was upon the cities, so too there all the nations feared them."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:43.011871615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}